 "known_limitations": [
  "Not an exact 3-D Boolean arrangement (\u00a77.3-7.4): F_safe is under-approximated by SAFE octree leaves + support-plane convex cells; completeness is resolution-bounded (a passage narrower than ~2 x min_cell_m=0.05 m may be missed -> UNKNOWN, never a false UNREACHABLE).",
  "UNREACHABLE needs a cut of boxes each inside ONE pair's inner polytope; a wall closed only by several inner polytopes at sub-min_cell scale stays UNKNOWN.",
  "Floating-point conservative certificates with declared slack (as gs3d); no exact/dyadic arithmetic.",
  "Cell-sequence choice by A* over portal samples is a heuristic (no GCS mixed-integer optimum); post-processing (cell-sequence SLSQP, certified shortcut/tighten/corner-merge) is local.",
  "Paths hug obstacles at margin + 1 mm buffer (like the baseline's ~0.0500 clearance); flight-grade safety margins, attitude, wind and dynamics are out of scope (Phase U0 only; no yaw product complex).",
  "The gs3d A6 smoother eases to a stop at every anchor, so its jerk metric depends on anchor count/spacing as much as on geometric smoothness; report turning/curvature metrics alongside it.",
  "Compile timings were measured on shared cpu_short nodes; not a controlled benchmark.",
  "UNREACHABLE is certified inside the declared query box: the N2 start component is bounded by the plug/lamp/header slab, walls and floor, and by the box face u_min, which is air (same declared-domain assumption as the baseline; L1's B6/B6h moved that face and the route did not change)."
 ],
